<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="60249" href="schedule/2015/spring/STAT/430/60249.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2015" href="schedule/2015.xml">2015</calendarYear><term id="120151" href="schedule/2015/spring.xml">Spring 2015</term><subject id="STAT" href="schedule/2015/spring/STAT.xml">Statistics</subject><course id="430" href="schedule/2015/spring/STAT/430.xml">Topics in Applied Statistics</course></parents><sectionNumber>M1U</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Stochastic Processes</sectionTitle><creditHours>3 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>A stochastic process is a random process that represents the evolution of some system over time.  The course is aimed at advanced undergraduate and beginning graduate students.  Topics include discrete-time Markov chains, random walks, continuous-time Markov chains, Poisson processes, birth-and-death processes, renewal processes, queues, Brownian motion (Wiener process), and Ito's lemma.  Restricted to students majoring in Statistics or Statistics &amp; Computer Science until Dec 1, 2014.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Undergrad - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>CrossListOpen (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2015-01-20Z</startDate><endDate>2015-05-06Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>03:00 PM</start><end>03:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>MWF    </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>132</roomNumber><buildingName>Bevier Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Stepanov" firstName="A">Stepanov, A</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>